---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Your privacy">
  <article class="content-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">YOUR STUDIO, YOUR MATERIALS</p>
    <h1>Your privacy</h1>
    <p class="privacy-meta">Effective 25 October 2026</p>
    <p>
      Ahab stores the information needed to provide your account, generation
      service, payments and private library. Do not upload sensitive personal
      material that is unnecessary for your project.
    </p>
    <h2>What is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Your account includes your username, password hash, optional separately
      hashed recovery passcode and session records. Your library includes saved
      prompts, images, audio and video references, generated outputs and related
      metadata. Purchase and generation records support payment verification,
      allowances and troubleshooting.
    </p>
    <h2>Library limits and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Each account keeps up to 80 prompts, 40 images, 20 audio uploads, 10 video
      references and 23 generated videos. Adding a new item beyond a category’s
      limit removes its oldest item. Generated videos also expire after 121
      days. You can delete individual saved items from your library. Temporary
      processing copies and queued deletion retries may take additional time to
      clear.
    </p>
    <h2>Services used to deliver Ahab</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare hosts the application, account data and private media.
      OpenRouter and the selected model provider process the scripts and
      references you submit for generation. Their own service and retention
      terms apply to processing outside Ahab. Stripe handles checkout and
      payment details. Ahab does not store your card information.
    </p>
    <h2>Private access and cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Your media library requires account authorization. A secure, HTTP-only
      session cookie keeps you signed in for up to 270 days. Provider access
      links are time-limited. The installed app caches public static resources
      for its offline screen; it does not intentionally cache your authenticated
      pages, private media or API responses.
    </p>
    <h2>Keeping your account safe</h2>
    <p>
      You can change your password or optional recovery passcode in Security,
      sign out to revoke your session, and delete saved library items. Password
      resets revoke existing sessions. If no recovery passcode is set,
      signed-out account recovery is unavailable.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      For a purchase or privacy issue, use the merchant contact details on your
      Stripe receipt. Include your username or purchase reference without
      sharing your password or recovery passcode.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
